return [====[als max(0, CHA_MOD) supplemental magical damage to hostiles within 2 same-floor cell radius.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with a discrete active Magic Form</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 46</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_hitstun_presence" data-title="Unnerving Presence"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Unnerving Presence</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_1"><h3>Unnerving Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>After the ordinary CHA hit-stun multiplier is calculated, multiplies eligible hit stun inflicted by this actor by 1.10 total. Higher ranks replace lower ranks; ordinary retrigger guards, defender resistance, anti-stunlock rules, and hard caps remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_2"><h3>Dazing Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Unnerving Presence</p><p>After the ordinary CHA hit-stun multiplier is calculated, multiplies eligible hit stun inflicted by this actor by 1.20 total. Higher ranks replace lower ranks; ordinary retrigger guards, defender resistance, anti-stunlock rules, and hard caps remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_HITSTUN_3"><h3>Overwhelming Presence</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dazing Presence</p><p>After the ordinary CHA hit-stun multiplier is calculated, multiplies eligible hit stun inflicted by this actor by 1.30 total. Higher ranks replace lower ranks; ordinary retrigger guards, defender resistance, anti-stunlock rules, and hard caps remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible hit-stun source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 47</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_intimidation_proc" data-title="Daunting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Daunting</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_1"><h3>Daunting</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Sets IntimidationProcChance = 0.11. If an eligible target-hit event damages a surviving defender whose MoraleCheckCooldown is inactive and that same event did not already require a Morale check from an ordinary trauma trigger, a successful proc forces exactly one Morale check even when the hit would otherwise be below the defender&#x27;s trauma threshold. The ordinary attacker-CHA MoraleDC and defender-CHA MoraleSave formulas apply, and the normal controller-specific cooldown begins after that check whether it succeeds or fails.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_2"><h3>Cowing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Daunting</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets IntimidationProcChance = 0.22. If an eligible target-hit event damages a surviving defender whose MoraleCheckCooldown is inactive and that same event did not already require a Morale check from an ordinary trauma trigger, a successful proc forces exactly one Morale check even when the hit would otherwise be below the defender&#x27;s trauma threshold. The ordinary attacker-CHA MoraleDC and defender-CHA MoraleSave formulas apply, and the normal controller-specific cooldown begins after that check whether it succeeds or fails.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_FEAR_PROC_3"><h3>Overawing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Cowing</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets IntimidationProcChance = 0.33. If an eligible target-hit event damages a surviving defender whose MoraleCheckCooldown is inactive and that same event did not already require a Morale check from an ordinary trauma trigger, a successful proc forces exactly one Morale check even when the hit would otherwise be below the defender&#x27;s trauma threshold. The ordinary attacker-CHA MoraleDC and defender-CHA MoraleSave formulas apply, and the normal controller-specific cooldown begins after that check whether it succeeds or fails.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 48</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_menace" data-title="Menacing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Menacing</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_1"><h3>Menacing</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>This is rank 1 of the dedicated offensive intimidation family. Adds +2 to MoraleDC whenever this actor is the credited attacker for a Morale check. AI actors may acquire this family through the same ordinary deterministic FeatDirector eligibility and selection rules as other AI-legal feats whenever their CHA and prerequisites qualify; it is not reserved for player characters. Against a human-controlled defender, also set HumanMoraleTraumaFraction = 0.30 for damage credited to this actor, so a single hit dealing more than 30% of current MaxHP may trigger Morale instead of the ordinary greater-than-one-third requirement. This never enables the below-50%-HP trigger or repeated-below-half trigger against humans. Against AI defenders, trigger cadence remains the ordinary AI Morale cadence; Menacing improves the opposed check rather than creating extra checks.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_2"><h3>Dreadful</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Menacing</p><p>Replaces Menacing&#x27;s +2 with +4 total MoraleDC. Against human-controlled defenders, replaces Menacing&#x27;s trauma threshold with HumanMoraleTraumaFraction = 0.25, so a single hit dealing more than 25% of current MaxHP may trigger Morale. It still never enables a human below-50%-HP or repeated-below-half trigger. Dreadful replaces rather than stacks with Menacing&#x27;s threshold and DC bonus.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MENACE_3"><h3>Terrifying</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>Retains Dreadful&#x27;s +4 total MoraleDC. Against human-controlled defenders, replaces Dreadful&#x27;s trauma threshold with HumanMoraleTraumaFraction = 0.20, so a single hit dealing more than 20% of current MaxHP may trigger Morale; it still never enables the below-50%-HP or repeated-below-half trigger against humans. In addition, the first Morale Save each eligible defender makes against this actor during an encounter is rolled twice and the lower natural d20 is kept before modifiers. Later Morale Saves by that defender against the same actor return to one d20. Terrifying therefore specializes an actor into intimidation by widening the set of genuinely traumatic hits against human-controlled targets and making its first fear attempt especially difficult, while the defender&#x27;s controller-based Morale cooldown remains unchanged and continues to prevent repeated player lockout.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 49</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_nerve" data-title="Iron Nerve"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Iron Nerve</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_1"><h3>Iron Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Adds +2 to Morale Saves.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NERVE_2"><h3>Unbreakable Nerve</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Iron Nerve</p><p>Replaces Iron Nerve with a +4 Morale Save bonus.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors subject to Morale</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 50</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_panic" data-title="Panic Is Contagious"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Panic Is Contagious</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_PANIC"><h3>Panic Is Contagious</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Dreadful</p><p>After an enemy fails Morale against this actor, eligible AI hostiles below half health within two graph cells make one nonrecursive Morale check; each receives 3.0 seconds cascade immunity.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 51</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_personality_aura" data-title="Abrasive Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Abrasive Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_ABRASIVE_PERSONALITY_1"><h3>Abrasive Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 13</p><p>Every sealed non-exploding 3d4 seconds, deals max(0, CHA_MOD) untyped passive damage to hostiles within 0 same-floor cell radius.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_NARCISSISM_2"><h3>Narcissism</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / requires Abrasive Personality</p><p>Every sealed non-exploding 3d4 seconds, deals max(0, CHA_MOD) untyped passive damage to hostiles within 1 same-floor cell radius.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CHA_MEGALOMANIA_3"><h3>Megalomania</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17 / requires Narcissism</p><p>Every sealed non-exploding 3d4 seconds, deals max(0, CHA_MOD) untyped passive damage to hostiles within 2 same-floor cell radius.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 52</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_self_actualization" data-title="Self-Actualization"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Self-Actualization</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_SELF_ACTUALIZATION"><h3>Self-Actualization</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 15 / eligible Magic Form</p><p>Each eligible magical target damage event gains max(0, CHA_MOD) once after source-side multipliers.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an eligible attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 53</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cha_winning_personality" data-title="Winning Personality"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Winning Personality</h2><section class="entry" id="CHA_WINNING_PERSONALITY"><h3>Winning Personality</h3><p class="requirement">CHA 17</p><p>Permanently grants +1 intrinsic CHA, subject to the ordinary ability ceiling. For the printed ability-score prerequisite of INT-prefixed feats only, uses max(INT, CHA) after that increase. Actual INT and INT_MOD remain unchanged, and every prerequisite, restriction, capability, class exclusion, and availability rule remains authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 54</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_big_guy" data-title="Big Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BIG_GUY"><h3>Big Guy</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 and STR 13</p><p>Sets PlayerTargetScale to 1.30. Third-person/world presentation and combat hurt volume become 130% size while the authoritative movement/collision hull remains unchanged. Melee reach is multiplied by 1.15 and actor-authored physical push dealt is multiplied by 1.20. The larger hurt volume is the balancing drawback. Big Guy and Little Guy are mutually exclusive.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 55</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_blast_proof" data-title="Blast-Proof"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Blast-Proof</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_BLAST_PROOF"><h3>Blast-Proof</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Once every 2.0 seconds per defender, suppresses the first qualifying continuation created by an incoming actor-owned exploding damage die. The triggering die and all already-resolved damage remain; that continuation is omitted and its chain ends. Independent damage-die chains are unaffected.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 56</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_glow_up" data-title="Glow Up"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Glow Up</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_GLOW_UP"><h3>Glow Up</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires a usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p><p>Whenever an owned rule contributes max(0, CHA_MOD) as damage to a resolved damage event, adds max(0, CON_MOD) to that same event once. Requires a currently usable explicit CHA_MOD-derived damage source.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with an authored CHA_MOD-derived damage source</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 57</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_health_regeneration" data-title="Second Wind"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Second Wind</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_11"><h3>Second Wind</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Enables passive Health Regeneration. Adds 11% MaxHP to the regeneration ceiling; highest rank only. Stacks with a Fighter&#x27;s innate 33%. After 5.0 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1.0% MaxHP/second times the CON regeneration multiplier toward the combined ceiling. Never restores Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_22"><h3>Rapid Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Second Wind</p><p>Replaces lower Recovery ranks. Adds 22% MaxHP to the regeneration ceiling; highest rank only. Stacks with a Fighter&#x27;s innate 33%. After 5.0 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1.0% MaxHP/second times the CON regeneration multiplier toward the combined ceiling. Never restores Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_REGEN_33"><h3>Unbroken</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Rapid Recovery</p><p>Replaces lower Recovery ranks. Adds 33% MaxHP to the regeneration ceiling; highest rank only. Stacks with a Fighter&#x27;s innate 33%. After 5.0 damage-free seconds, regenerate 1.0% MaxHP/second times the CON regeneration multiplier toward the combined ceiling. Never restores Tetris overfill.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 58</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_not_yet" data-title="Not Yet"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Not Yet</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_NOT_YET"><h3>Not Yet</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15</p><p>Once per dungeon for each owning actor, damage that would reduce the actor from above 1 HP to 0 or less instead leaves that actor at exactly 1 HP and grants 0.50 seconds of damage immunity. The trigger is consumed for that dungeon even if the actor is healed, dies later, respawns, disconnects/reconnects, or changes floors; it resets only when the campaign advances to a new dungeon. An AI actor spawned for the first time in a dungeon begins with its one use available and cannot gain another use within that dungeon through despawn/recreation exploits.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 59</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_poison_proc" data-title="Venomous"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Venomous</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_1"><h3>Venomous</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Sets PoisonProcChance = 0.11. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one poison-status application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s CON for PoisonDC and the defender&#x27;s CON for PoisonSave. A failed save applies the canonical Poisoned state; a successful save prevents it. Existing Poisoned reapplication/recovery rules remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_2"><h3>Toxic</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15 / requires Venomous</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets PoisonProcChance = 0.22. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one poison-status application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s CON for PoisonDC and the defender&#x27;s CON for PoisonSave. A failed save applies the canonical Poisoned state; a successful save prevents it. Existing Poisoned reapplication/recovery rules remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="CON_POISON_PROC_3"><h3>Virulent</h3><p class="requirement">CON 17 / requires Toxic</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets PoisonProcChance = 0.33. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one poison-status application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s CON for PoisonDC and the defender&#x27;s CON for PoisonSave. A failed save applies the canonical Poisoned state; a successful save prevents it. Existing Poisoned reapplication/recovery rules remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 60</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-con_steadfast" data-title="Hard to Move"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hard to Move</h2><section class="entry" id="CON_STEADFAST"><h3>Hard to Move</h3><p class="requirement">CON 13</p><p>Incoming ordinary hit-stun duration and non-scripted push displacement are each multiplied by 0.75. Authored boss mechanics that explicitly ignore resistance remain exceptions.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 61</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_big_scary" data-title="Big Scary"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Big Scary</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BIG_SCARY"><h3>Big Scary</h3><p class="requirement">CON 15, STR 13, and CHA 15 / Big Guy; Menacing</p><p>When this actor deals melee damage or a physical push/wall-crush event, that event&#x27;s MoraleDC gains an additional +2. It stacks with the Menacing family and exists specifically to make an intimidating giant bruiser build possible without changing ordinary ranged intimidation.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 62</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_boom_battery" data-title="Boom Battery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Boom Battery</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_BOOM_BATTERY"><h3>Boom Battery</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and INT 15 / Capability: exploding_nonmagic_damage_dice</p><p>Actor-owned non-Magic damage Boomchains may now feed Magic: every second continuation die generated by the same non-Magic attack restores 1 Magic, up to 5 Magic per attack event. This does not alter explosion thresholds and never raises Magic above 100.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 63</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_crush_panic" data-title="Crash the Party"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Crash the Party</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_CRUSH_PANIC"><h3>Crash the Party</h3><p class="requirement">STR 17 and CHA 17 / Pusher; Dreadful</p><p>A wall crush caused by this actor immediately requests a Morale check from the crushed target if it is otherwise morale-eligible, even if its normal one-second Morale recheck gate has not elapsed. This special request has a 3.0-second per-target cooldown. Other morale eligibility, immunity, and flee rules remain unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with physical push</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 64</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_force_of_will" data-title="Force of Will"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Force of Will</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_FORCE_OF_WILL"><h3>Force of Will</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and WIS 15 / Pusher; Force Multiplier</p><p>The actor&#x27;s Magic-origin pushes are additionally eligible for Pusher/Shover/Space Hog processing as already-pushing events. Force Multiplier resolves first; then, only when that attacker-target pair is not inside the shared 0.50-second PusherProcTargetCooldown, the Pusher-family proc may add its +168-world-unit physical displacement on success, and any resulting valid wall slam uses the actor&#x27;s active Pusher-family wall-slam die. Force of Will does not make non-pushing Magic damage eligible for a Pusher proc. This is an explicit bridge feat; without it the physical-weapon Pusher family and magic_push family remain separate.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, eligible AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 65</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_meteor_strike" data-title="Meteor Strike"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Meteor Strike</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_METEOR_STRIKE"><h3>Meteor Strike</h3><p class="requirement">STR 15 and INT 15 / Bash; Cloud Step</p><p>Once per airborne cycle, a Crowbar-family hit made after consuming Cloud Step&#x27;s feat-granted second jump and before legitimate ground contact adds one extra 1d6 physical-damage chain and doubles that hit&#x27;s Crowbar-origin push distance before other compatible push multipliers. The bonus d6 obeys the universal exploding rule. Missing the swing does not consume the once-per-airborne-cycle strike; landing resets it.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers with Crowbar-family access</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 66</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-cross_tiny_terror" data-title="Tiny Terror"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Tiny Terror</h2><section class="entry" id="CROSS_TINY_TERROR"><h3>Tiny Terror</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 and CHA 15 / Little Guy; Menacing</p><p>While Little Guy is active, MoraleDC gains an additional +2 against enemies within 2 graph cells of the actor. This stacks with the Menacing family but applies only at close range.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 67</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_burst_size" data-title="Extra Round"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extra Round</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_1"><h3>Extra Round</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets BurstBonusRounds = +1 total for attacks already authored as multiFireBurst. Added projectiles inherit the weapon&#x27;s existing burst spacing, damage, and ammunition semantics; they never create extra ammo costs or turn single-fire attacks, Shotgun pellets, penetration, exploding dice, or unrelated extra-projectile procs into bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_2"><h3>Extended Volley</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Extra Round</p><p>Sets BurstBonusRounds = +2 total for attacks already authored as multiFireBurst. Added projectiles inherit the weapon&#x27;s existing burst spacing, damage, and ammunition semantics; they never create extra ammo costs or turn single-fire attacks, Shotgun pellets, penetration, exploding dice, or unrelated extra-projectile procs into bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_BURSTER_3"><h3>Full Barrage</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Extended Volley</p><p>Sets BurstBonusRounds = +3 total for attacks already authored as multiFireBurst. Added projectiles inherit the weapon&#x27;s existing burst spacing, damage, and ammunition semantics; they never create extra ammo costs or turn single-fire attacks, Shotgun pellets, penetration, exploding dice, or unrelated extra-projectile procs into bursts.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI actors with an authored weapon attack tagged multiFireBurst</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 68</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_clumsy_proc" data-title="Distracting"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Distracting</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_1"><h3>Distracting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets ClumsyProcChance = 0.11. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one clumsy-tagged application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ClumsyDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ClumsySave. A failed save applies canonical Clumsy; a successful save prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_2"><h3>Disorienting</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Distracting</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ClumsyProcChance = 0.22. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one clumsy-tagged application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ClumsyDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ClumsySave. A failed save applies canonical Clumsy; a successful save prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_CLUMSY_PROC_3"><h3>Discombobulating</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Disorienting</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ClumsyProcChance = 0.33. On an eligible target-hit event under the common status-proc rules, a successful proc creates one clumsy-tagged application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ClumsyDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ClumsySave. A failed save applies canonical Clumsy; a successful save prevents it.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 69</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_exploding_damage_dice" data-title="Perfect Ten"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Perfect Ten</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D10"><h3>Perfect Ten</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Makes ordinary actor-owned d10 damage dice explode. Fresh d10 dice explode only on natural 10; continuation dice use threshold max(2, 10 - BoomShift). The unlock is additive with earlier ranks and every chain obeys the universal 32-die cap.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d10 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D8"><h3>Eight Is Enough</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Perfect Ten</p><p>Makes ordinary actor-owned d8 damage dice explode. Fresh d8 dice explode only on natural 8; continuation dice use threshold max(2, 8 - BoomShift). The unlock is additive with earlier ranks and every chain obeys the universal 32-die cap.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d8 damage rolls</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_EXPLODE_D4"><h3>Fourtunate</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Eight Is Enough</p><p>Makes ordinary actor-owned d4 damage dice explode. Fresh d4 dice explode only on natural 4; continuation dice use threshold max(2, 4 - BoomShift). The unlock is additive with earlier ranks and every chain obeys the universal 32-die cap.</p><p class="actors">Non-Rogue heroes, human Soldiers, and AI with d4 damage rolls</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 70</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_immolate_proc" data-title="Singeing"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Singeing</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_1"><h3>Singeing</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets ImmolateProcChance = 0.11. On an eligible target-hit under the shared Status-proc feat-family rules, a successful proc creates exactly one Immolated application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateSave. A successful save prevents ignition. If that attack already guarantees an Immolated save through an authored fire/immolate rule, skip this redundant proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_2"><h3>Scorching</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Singeing</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ImmolateProcChance = 0.22. On an eligible target-hit under the shared Status-proc feat-family rules, a successful proc creates exactly one Immolated application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateSave. A successful save prevents ignition. If that attack already guarantees an Immolated save through an authored fire/immolate rule, skip this redundant proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_IMMOLATE_PROC_3"><h3>Incendiary</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Scorching</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ImmolateProcChance = 0.33. On an eligible target-hit under the shared Status-proc feat-family rules, a successful proc creates exactly one Immolated application attempt using the attacker&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateDC and the defender&#x27;s DEX for ImmolateSave. A successful save prevents ignition. If that attack already guarantees an Immolated save through an authored fire/immolate rule, skip this redundant proc roll.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 71</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_magnum_deadeye" data-title="Deadeye"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Deadeye</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_MAGNUM_DEADEYE"><h3>Deadeye</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Deadeye enables Aim State for all standard damage-capable player weapons. A completed aim (0.50 seconds of perfect stillness) empowers exactly one next primary attack transaction for x2 damage. If the weapon is the .357 Magnum (which natively supports x2 aim), Deadeye empowers it to x3.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled actors using a standard player weapon</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 72</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_rate_of_fire" data-title="Hair Trigger"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Hair Trigger</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_1"><h3>Hair Trigger</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets RateOfFireMultiplier = 1.10 total. Eligible ordinary-firearm primary attack intervals are divided by this multiplier; reloads, Magic cooldowns, SMG cooling/overheat lockout, AR2 targeting-laser duration, internal AR2 three-shot spacing, Magnum free-projectile burst spacing, and enemy telegraphs are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_2"><h3>Rapid Fire</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Hair Trigger</p><p>Sets RateOfFireMultiplier = 1.20 total. Eligible ordinary-firearm primary attack intervals are divided by this multiplier; reloads, Magic cooldowns, SMG cooling/overheat lockout, AR2 targeting-laser duration, internal AR2 three-shot spacing, Magnum free-projectile burst spacing, and enemy telegraphs are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_RATE_OF_FIRE_3"><h3>Lead Storm</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Rapid Fire</p><p>Sets RateOfFireMultiplier = 1.30 total. Eligible ordinary-firearm primary attack intervals are divided by this multiplier; reloads, Magic cooldowns, SMG cooling/overheat lockout, AR2 targeting-laser duration, internal AR2 three-shot spacing, Magnum free-projectile burst spacing, and enemy telegraphs are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and AI whose equipped/authored ordinary firearm uses the shared attack-cadence authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 73</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_reload_cadence" data-title="Quick Reload"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Quick Reload</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD"><h3>Quick Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets ReloadTimeMultiplier = 0.80 for ordinary reloadable weapons. It changes only genuine reload timing and never shortens SMG overheat recovery, AR2 targeting-laser/burst timing, Magic cooldowns, burst-internal spacing, or enemy telegraphs.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_2"><h3>Lightning Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Quick Reload</p><p>Sets ReloadTimeMultiplier = 0.60 for ordinary reloadable weapons. It changes only genuine reload timing and never shortens SMG overheat recovery, AR2 targeting-laser/burst timing, Magic cooldowns, burst-internal spacing, or enemy telegraphs.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_FAST_RELOAD_3"><h3>Blink Reload</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Lightning Reload</p><p>Sets ReloadTimeMultiplier = 0.40 for ordinary reloadable weapons. It changes only genuine reload timing and never shortens SMG overheat recovery, AR2 targeting-laser/burst timing, Magic cooldowns, burst-internal spacing, or enemy telegraphs.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes/human Soldiers; AI only when its authored weapon uses the shared reload authority</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 74</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_shrink" data-title="Little Guy"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Little Guy</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SHRINK"><h3>Little Guy</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Sets PlayerTargetScale to 0.70 while preserving the ordinary authoritative collision hull, stair legality, USE reach, weapon traces, and progression interactions.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 75</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_smg_heat" data-title="Cold Hands"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cold Hands</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_1"><h3>Cold Hands</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Sets SMGHeatSuppressionChance = 0.11 and SMGOverheatThreshold = 8. Every successful SMG round makes one server-authoritative deterministic suppression roll before its ordinary +1 heat; success adds 0 heat. Damage, ammunition, firing cadence, sub-threshold cooling, visual/audio feedback, and the fixed 2.0-second overheat lockout are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_2"><h3>Ice in the Veins</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15 / requires Cold Hands</p><p>Replaces lower Cold Hands ranks and sets SMGHeatSuppressionChance = 0.22 and SMGOverheatThreshold = 10. Every successful SMG round makes one server-authoritative deterministic suppression roll before its ordinary +1 heat; success adds 0 heat. Damage, ammunition, firing cadence, sub-threshold cooling, visual/audio feedback, and the fixed 2.0-second overheat lockout are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SMG_COLD_HANDS_3"><h3>Absolute Zero</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 17 / requires Ice in the Veins</p><p>Replaces lower Cold Hands ranks and sets SMGHeatSuppressionChance = 0.33 and SMGOverheatThreshold = 12. Every successful SMG round makes one server-authoritative deterministic suppression roll before its ordinary +1 heat; success adds 0 heat. Damage, ammunition, firing cadence, sub-threshold cooling, visual/audio feedback, and the fixed 2.0-second overheat lockout are unchanged.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers who possess/use the SMG</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 76</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_spring_heel" data-title="Spring Heel"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Spring Heel</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_SPRING_HEEL"><h3>Spring Heel</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 13</p><p>Doubles the apex height of every voluntary jump generated by the actor, including ordinary ground jump and Cloud Step&#x27;s feat-granted second jump. Under unchanged gravity, takeoff vertical impulse is scaled to achieve 2.0x baseline jump height. Push, knockback, falls, scripted relocation, ladders, stairs, and other non-jump movement are unchanged; anti-top, gate, ceiling, and progression blockers remain authoritative.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 77</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_strafe" data-title="Strafer"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Strafer</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_STRAFER_1"><h3>Strafer</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Ordinary lateral strafe movement is 11% faster. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. Highest rank replaces lower ranks; jumping, airborne, ladder and forced movement are unchanged.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_SIDELER_2"><h3>Sideler</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Ordinary lateral strafe movement is 22% faster. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. Highest rank replaces lower ranks; jumping, airborne, ladder and forced movement are unchanged.</p></section><section class="entry" id="DEX_LATERAL_MOVER_3"><h3>Lateral Mover</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Ordinary lateral strafe movement is 33% faster. Only the sideways component changes on diagonals. Highest rank replaces lower ranks; jumping, airborne, ladder and forced movement are unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 78</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-dex_wall_jump" data-title="Wall Jump"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Wall Jump</h2><section class="entry" id="DEX_WALL_JUMP"><h3>Wall Jump</h3><p class="requirement">DEX 15</p><p>Kick off a wall up to four times before landing. Each fresh Jump press within 24 units of a static vertical wall (including maze walls) gives an ordinary jump and a kick away. No Magic cost. Landing restores all four kicks; wall contact does not. Spring Heel improves the jump height.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 79</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_ammo_regeneration_floor" data-title="Field Supply"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Field Supply</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_44"><h3>Field Supply</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Replaces lower ammo-regeneration ranks and sets ordinary regenerative firearm AmmoRegenFloorFraction to 0.44; each owned eligible family stops at ceil(MaxFamilyCapacity × 0.44) without changing capacity, cadence, no-fire delay, consumables, or AR2 secondary ammunition.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_55"><h3>Deep Reserves</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Field Supply</p><p>Replaces lower ammo-regeneration ranks and sets ordinary regenerative firearm AmmoRegenFloorFraction to 0.55; each owned eligible family stops at ceil(MaxFamilyCapacity × 0.55) without changing capacity, cadence, no-fire delay, consumables, or AR2 secondary ammunition.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_AMMO_FLOOR_66"><h3>War Stock</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Deep Reserves</p><p>Replaces lower ammo-regeneration ranks and sets ordinary regenerative firearm AmmoRegenFloorFraction to 0.66; each owned eligible family stops at ceil(MaxFamilyCapacity × 0.66) without changing capacity, cadence, no-fire delay, consumables, or AR2 secondary ammunition.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled heroes and human Soldiers with regenerative firearm ammunition</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 80</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arc_recovery" data-title="Arc Recovery"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Arc Recovery</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARC_RECOVERY"><h3>Arc Recovery</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / magic_pool</p><p>Defeating an AI hostile with a Magic-tagged damage event restores 5 Magic, subject to one 2.0-second per-actor internal cooldown and the universal 100-Magic ceiling.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 81</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_arcane_disruption_proc" data-title="Disruptor"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Disruptor</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_1"><h3>Disruptor</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13</p><p>Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.11. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_2"><h3>Spellbreaker</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / requires Disruptor</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.22. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><section class="entry" id="INT_ARCANE_PROC_3"><h3>Nullifier</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / requires Spellbreaker</p><p>Replaces lower ranks. Sets ArcaneDisruptionProcChance = 0.33. When an eligible physical=true, magical=false target-hit event damages a surviving target whose Arcane Shield is online, a successful proc forces exactly one post-damage Arcane Integrity save using the ordinary attacker-INT ArcaneBreakDC and defender-INT ArcaneIntegritySave formulas. This does not retag the underlying damage as magical. The physical hit remains ordinarily Feedback-eligible, and any Feedback resolution from that hit completes before this proc-created Arcane Integrity save. Magical hits do not roll this family because they already force Arcane Integrity saves automatically.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, AI with an eligible attributable damaging attack</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 82</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_backpedal" data-title="W,A,S,Deborah"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>W,A,S,Deborah</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_WAS_DEBORAH"><h3>W,A,S,Deborah</h3><p class="requirement"></p><p>Voluntary backward movement, including backward diagonals, is 25% faster. Composes with ordinary movement modes and map movement. Forward movement, pure strafing, jumping and forced motion are unchanged.</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 83</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_cloud_step" data-title="Cloud Step"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Cloud Step</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_CLOUD_STEP"><h3>Cloud Step</h3><p class="requirement">INT 13 / Magic pool</p><p>Once per airborne cycle, a fresh Space press may spend exactly 5 Magic for one additional voluntary jump. A valid Wall Jump with a remaining use has priority and leaves Cloud Step unused.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 84</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_extracurricular_activity" data-title="Extracurricular Activity"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Extracurricular Activity</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_EXTRACURRICULAR_ACTIVITY"><h3>Extracurricular Activity</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic content</p><p>Immediately grants one deterministic distinct canonical Magic content without replacing later scheduled grants.</p><p class="actors">Cooperative Heroes only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 85</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_feedback_loop" data-title="Feedback Loop"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Feedback Loop</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FEEDBACK_LOOP"><h3>Feedback Loop</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / magic_pool</p><p>Every continuation die actually generated by an offensive Magic attack restores 1 Magic to its caster, capped at 6 restored Magic per committed cast/attack event. Initial dice and unbridged weapon-only Boomchains never count.</p><p class="actors">Heroes, human Soldiers, and Magic-using AI</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 86</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_float_on" data-title="Float On"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Float On</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_FLOAT_ON"><h3>Float On</h3><p class="requirement">INT 15 / Magic pool</p><p>Once per airborne cycle, hold Space at the apex for a controllable float of up to 3.0 seconds, spending exactly 5 Magic per second. It ends on release, ground contact, exhaustion, or cap.</p><p class="actors">Player-controlled Heroes and human Soldiers only</p></section><div class="folio">THE LEGEND OF DEBORAH · 87</div></article><article class="page" id="feat-int_grand_unified_theory" data-title="Grand Unified Theory"><div class="kicker">Feat reference</div><h2>Grand Unified Theory</h2><section class="entry" id="INT_GRAND_UNIFIED_THEORY"><h3>Grand Unified Theory</h3><p class="requirement">INT 17 / unowned Magic form</p><p>Immediately grants one deterministic distinct canonical Magic form without replacing later scheduled grants.<]====]
